cgtree (0.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial Debian package.
  * First release of cgtree, a CLI for inspecting the cgroup v2 hierarchy.
    Running cgtree with no arguments opens the interactive explorer on a
    terminal and falls back to list output when piped.
  * list: print the hierarchy as a tree on stdout, with --depth to limit
    levels and --format text|json to choose between the tree rendering and a
    JSON document of every node and its interface files.
  * explore: interactive terminal explorer with expand/collapse navigation,
    expand-all and collapse-all, rescan, and an in-app help screen.
  * Property display: --props shows cgroup interface files alongside each
    node, matched by comma-separated substring patterns ("*" for all); the
    explorer applies the same matching live via 'p' and 'f'.
  * --root inspects a hierarchy other than /sys/fs/cgroup. cgroup v1 hosts are
    reported as unsupported, and unreadable directories are shown as leaves
    rather than aborting the scan.
  * Ships man pages and bash, zsh and fish completions.

 -- Mykolas Krupauskas <m.krupauskas@gmail.com>  Sat, 19 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
